== FINDINGS (observations for design review round 10) ==
  F1 (contradiction). Edge Case 16 D17's second clause ('an axis is set while the story position is before its lock scene's commit'; a position inside a lock scene counts as before it) is not limited to loaded records, unlike D9. The live crisis record — Deleted set by T4, nothing stored, position inside C8-S16 — therefore satisfies D17, and storyline_phase() returns DAMAGED instead of CRISIS for every live crisis (the Formulas' own example '(NONE, ARCHIVE, RELEASE, nothing stored, OUTSIDE) -> CRISIS' with loaded false fails). Candidate repair (the 'repaired' run above, all assertions PASS): test D17's before-commit clause on a loaded record only, like D9.
  F2 (AC wording). Axes AC9 expects load_check() of the CRISIS fixture to be exactly {D9}. The fixture must be positioned inside C8-S16 (the only place a crisis exists), so D17 fires too: phase DAMAGED, load_check ['D17', 'D9']. This holds under either reading (load_check always tests a loaded record). Candidate: AC9 says {D9, D17} for the CRISIS fixture.
  F3 (redundant clause). D17's prefix clause never fires alone: whenever the set axes are not a prefix of the lock order, either an UNSET axis sits behind the position (D16) or a set axis is ahead of it (D17 before-commit); the exhaustive check above found 0 counter-example(s). AC9's 'one fixture per clause' can only isolate it in combination with D17's other clause (same item, so 'exactly {D17}' still passes). Candidate: drop the prefix clause or keep it as documentation.
  F4 (AC9 fixtures). No single-field defect of a reachable save gives load_check exactly {item} for: D7.new_mismatch. D7.new_mismatch: changing a retraction entry's `new` also breaks the beat it implies (D14 under the model's strict 'matching': beat id = retract_<rule of the row before>_<axis>_<new>), and changing the record's axis value breaks the ID (D1). D14 does not define 'matching'. Under a looser reading (a beat matches an entry with the same axis) the same fixture gives exactly {D7}: confirmed by the model. Decide 'matching', or let AC9's D7 fixture also report D14. AC9 asks for one fixture per clause.
  F5 (load-check gaps; debug or edited saves only). load_check accepts records no play writes (counts are single-field changes summed over signatures): retraction withdrawn_item 28672; retraction scene 28672; lock_negotiated toggle 203264; seed flag toggle 212224; axis faction 5376; axis authority 4608. Nothing compares `lock_negotiated` with lock_pass() of the saved seeds (an edited save can turn sole_dissent on or off, and a changed Faction or Authority value before C8-S16 keeps the old lock_negotiated), and nothing compares a retraction entry's withdrawn item or scene with the retraction table. None of these records strands the player (forward walk above), so they are content-integrity gaps, not soft-locks. Edge Case 16 does not claim to catch them; decide whether that is acceptable or add D-items.
  F6 (D7 is one-directional). A record with a retraction_log entry (and its beat) but an empty axis_revised passes load_check: D7 requires every revised axis to be named by an entry, not every entry's axis to be revised (28672 such records accepted). The composer reads axis_revised. Candidate: D7 clause 'a retraction_log entry whose axis is not in axis_revised'.
  F7 (position vs root_phase). No Edge Case 16 item ties root_phase to the story position: 404992 position changes and 143360 root_phase changes of reachable saves load, e.g. an INSIDE record positioned in Chapter 9, a FINAL record positioned before the boss, an OUTSIDE (VALIDATED) record inside Root of Heaven, and records positioned inside a suppression window (FINAL_AUTH_OPEN, S13_OPEN, S14_OPEN, S16_OPEN): load_check does not enforce I9's 'no save is positioned inside a lock scene'. Some strand the player (see above).
  F8 (L-AC8 coverage). L-AC8's load path lists LEANING, PARTLY_LOCKED, FIXED and FINAL outcomes but no VALIDATED cell; a VALIDATED save positioned inside Root of Heaven cannot be written by play (T7 is atomic) yet passes load_check, and the load-path gate then runs T7. The model treats this as acceptable; the lifecycle could say so.
  F9 (dead transition). T6 (TURNED_BACK) can never fire. The story path reaches the gate only after the Chapter 9 end and the world-map path only once Root of Heaven is on the map, so every record at the gate is positioned past C8-S16; with an UNSET axis that position satisfies D16, and storyline_phase() (which runs the damaged-record check first, on live records too) returns DAMAGED, not LEANING or PARTLY_LOCKED. The walk never fires T6, and L-AC8's synthetic story-path cells for LEANING and PARTLY_LOCKED cannot be set up: a fixture save there is refused on load (D16), and a live record there meets the gate as DAMAGED, a phase the gate table has no row for. Candidates: (a) keep T6 as a defensive row and give the gate a DAMAGED row (TURNED_BACK, or a data error), with L-AC8 testing it by injecting a live record; or (b) drop T6 and the two L-AC8 cells, since D16 already guarantees them unreachable.
  F10 (load check vs Story+; edited saves only). 61440 accepted records cannot reach FINAL, all of them a record whose root_phase is not FINAL positioned after the final authorization's commit (FINAL_DONE, Story+). load_check accepts them (no item ties root_phase to the position, F7), and once in Story+ the model has no route back to the final authorization (modelling choice M8), so the ending is never confirmed. Play never writes them (T9 commits root_phase FINAL with its checkpoint). Candidate D-item: 'root_phase is not FINAL at a position past the final authorization's commit, or FINAL before it'.

== Modelling choices (where the GDDs leave the model a reading) ==
  M1 Seed contexts hold the 13 axis-seed flags only: modifier and timing rows are not read by lock_pass or load_check (except D15, which play cannot reach because set_story_flag clears the group). Seeds are fixed before C8-S13 (Act 1); side-arc flags join after Y2-PP-T17 maps them (AC15) and are not modelled.
  M2 Contexts are walked once per lock_pass signature: the transitions read seeds only through lock_pass.
  M3 A save is any reachable state outside the four suppression windows, plus every checkpoint. A quit or crash reloads an earlier save, which is a reachable state already in the walk, so reload edges add no states; A1/A2 check every save's load.
  M4 The `world_map` path is modelled only for re-entry (after leaving Root of Heaven, and from Story+); before the Chapter 9 end Root of Heaven is not on the map (lifecycle S6).
  M5 Positions are coarse: Chapter 9 is one position; the boss is one event (ROOT -> final authorization). A crisis-time save would sit at S16_OPEN.
  M6 D14 'matching' = the beat id retract_<rule of the row before the renegotiation>_<axis>_<new>; D1's four clauses are tagged in the order secret, UNSET axis, invalid row, other ID.
  M7 In 1.0 the invocation input I is always false (no source exists); every knob is false. Knob values are read only by formula_id at C8-S16 and the gate, so A6 also covers a mid-play knob patch.
  M8 Story+ (after T9) offers no route back to the boss or the final authorization; re-entering Root of Heaven from Story+ is T8 only. Whether Story+ can replay the boss belongs to the combat system (lifecycle Open Question 2).
  M9 The accepted-record probe applies one field change to every reachable save (both readings' saves are the same); 'accepted' means load_check is empty and no play in the mutated seed signature writes that (record, position).

